Chapter: DeskSheetStateTest
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopSheet
  cites Sheets chapter CellView
  cites Foreword chapter CCE

 The field the desk carries a sheet in. `da-sheet` is what makes an edit
 outlive a repaint, and until the Sheets pane paints from its own step
 the desk's tree arm still builds a fresh pane, so the two lines below
 are what says the field is real and typed rather than merely declared.

 THE EMPTY RECORD MUST CARRY None. Both close paths hand
 `desk-apps-empty` down when the mark stack is empty, and a field born
 holding a pane would hand a closed pane's memory to the next app.

 THE SECOND LINE IS THE ONE A SABOTAGE MOVES. A record built with a pane
 typed 5 into B2 must hand back THAT pane: reading D2 out of the tree
 built from `da-sheet` answers 1250, where a field carrying a fresh pane,
 or a reader that rebuilds one, answers 750.

Section: Body

  dss-kind-text : WidgetNode -> Text
  dss-kind-text (n) =
    when n.wn-kind
      is WkLabel (t) -> t
      is otherwise -> "<not a label>"

  dss-tree-cell : SheetPane, Integer, Integer -> Text
  dss-tree-cell (sp) (r) (c) =
    when widget-find (gsh-tree sp) ("sh-c-" & show r & "-" & show c)
      is Just (n) -> dss-kind-text n
      is None -> "<absent>"

  dss-held : DeskApps, Integer, Integer -> Text
  dss-held (apps) (r) (c) =
    when apps.da-sheet
      is Just (sp) -> dss-tree-cell sp r c
      is None -> "<no sheet held>"

  dss-typed : SheetPane, Integer, Integer, Text -> SheetPane
  dss-typed (sp) (r) (c) (txt) =
    SheetPane { sp-sheet = sheet-type (sp.sp-sheet) r c txt, sp-row = sp.sp-row, sp-col = sp.sp-col, sp-buf = sp.sp-buf }

 AND THE BODY IS DRAWN FROM THE PANE, WHICH IS THE HALF THE RECORD CANNOT
 SAY. `desk-sheet-body` renders into the window's content box and hands
 back the LAID tree, so reading D2 out of what it returns asks the
 question a person asks by looking at the window: not "does the desk hold
 a sheet" but "is the sheet on the glass the one the desk holds". A body
 that rebuilt its own sheet answers 750 here while the record line above
 stays green, which is why both lines exist.

 The chrome must no longer draw the grid, or two painters race and
 whichever ran last wins. `desk-wnd-tree`'s sheet arm answers the same
 empty panel the five heavy panes get, and an empty panel is a panel with
 no children rather than an absent one.

  dss-w : Integer = 800
  dss-h : Integer = 600

 THE CAPTURE GEOMETRY, because the two boxes are compared at the size the
 photograph is taken and a scale step sits at 1600.

  dss-big-w : Integer = 1600
  dss-big-h : Integer = 900

  dss-laid-cell : WidgetNode, Integer, Integer -> Text
  dss-laid-cell (laid) (r) (c) =
    when widget-find laid ("sh-c-" & show r & "-" & show c)
      is Just (n) -> dss-kind-text n
      is None -> "<absent>"

 THE HIT TEST IS CHECKED AGAINST THE PAINTER, NOT AGAINST ITSELF. The
 cell's rectangle comes from the tree `desk-sheet-body` actually laid;
 its centre goes to `desk-sheet-hit`, which lays the tree again and asks
 which widget the pointer is over. The two roads have to name the same
 cell, and a test that took the rectangle from the hit test's own lay
 could not tell you when they part.

 A LAID BOUND IS LOGICAL AND A POINTER IS DEVICE, and mixing them is
 invisible at 800 wide where the scale is 1. That is why this arm runs at
 1600, where the scale is 2 and the two spaces disagree by a factor: the
 centre is multiplied by the scale before it is offered as a pointer, and
 without that the hit answers -1 while every other line stays green.

 THE SECOND LINE IS THE CONTROL AND IT IS THE POINT. The same pointer
 offset by the content box's origin is what a tree laid at the SCREEN
 CORNER would have been asked, and it must answer a DIFFERENT cell. That
 is the failure the register warns about: the grid repaints with a cell
 highlighted and it looks exactly like a click that worked.

  dss-centre-x : WidgetNode, Text -> Integer
  dss-centre-x (laid) (id) =
    when widget-find laid id
      is Just (n) -> (n.wn-bounds).lr-x + (n.wn-bounds).lr-w / 2
      is None -> 0 - 1

  dss-centre-y : WidgetNode, Text -> Integer
  dss-centre-y (laid) (id) =
    when widget-find laid id
      is Just (n) -> (n.wn-bounds).lr-y + (n.wn-bounds).lr-h / 2
      is None -> 0 - 1

  dss-tone : WidgetNode, Text -> Integer
  dss-tone (laid) (id) =
    when widget-find laid id
      is Just (n) -> n.wn-tone
      is None -> 0 - 1

 TYPING IS ASSERTED THROUGH THE EVALUATOR, not against the buffer. B3
 holds 2 and D3 is =B3*C3 over 400, so D3 reads 800; typing 9 into B3 and
 committing must make D3 read 3600. A test that only read the buffer back
 would pass while `sheet-type` was never called, and a cell that shows
 what was typed but computes nothing is the failure that matters.

 The arm PRINTS the character the scancode produced rather than assuming
 it: the layout is `scancode-to-keycode`'s to decide, and an arm that
 hardcodes both sides of that mapping tests nothing about it.

  dss-cell-text : SheetPane, Integer, Integer -> Text
  dss-cell-text (sp) (r) (c) =
    let rs = eval-run ((sp.sp-sheet).sh-prog)
    in eval-cell ((sp.sp-sheet).sh-prog) rs r c

 SHEET-13 IS ASKED HERE RATHER THAN FROM A CAPTURE. Both roads paint into
 a scratch framebuffer of their own and the same pixel is read out of
 each: `dk-wnd-frame` is the road the chrome took before the pane painted
 its own body, and `desk-sheet-body` is the road it takes now. A capture
 could only say the two differ; this says WHERE, one row at a time, for
 the price of no guest at all.

  dss-px : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  dss-px (buf) (x) (y) = peek-32 buf ((y * dss-big-w + x) * 4)

  dss-row-of : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  dss-row-of (a) (b) (y) =
    "y " & show y & "  frame " & hex-i32 (dss-px a 800 y) & "  body " & hex-i32 (dss-px b 800 y)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing = act
    let held = DeskApps { da-files = None, da-browser = None, da-scene = None, da-edit = None, da-sheet = Just (dss-typed (gsh-pane-new 0) 1 1 "5"), da-review = None }
    in let ds = alloc-zeroed dk-ds-bytes 64
    in let blk = alloc-zeroed 64 64
    in let p = poke-32 ds dk-sheet-cell blk
    in let font = cbf-init
    in let buf = alloc-zeroed (dss-w * dss-h * 4) 64
    in let edited = dss-typed (gsh-pane-new blk) 1 1 "5"
    in act
      print-line-uni ("the empty record holds no sheet: [" & dss-held desk-apps-empty 1 3 & "]")
      print-line-uni ("and a record built around a pane typed 5 into B2 hands that pane back, D2 = [" & dss-held held 1 3 & "]")
      let laid = desk-sheet-body buf dss-w dss-h dss-w font gfont-none ds edited
      in print-line-uni ("the body draws the pane the desk holds, D2 on the glass = [" & dss-laid-cell laid 1 3 & "]")
      chrome <- desk-wnd-tree desk-focus-sheet ds buf dss-w dss-h dss-w gfont-none
      print-line-uni ("and the chrome draws no grid of its own, its children: " & show (chrome.wn-child-count))
      let box = dk-wnd-content desk-focus-sheet dss-w dss-h ds gfont-none (ui-wscale dss-w)
      in let lb = laid.wn-bounds
      in print-line-uni ("content box " & show (box.lr-x) & "," & show (box.lr-y) & " " & show (box.lr-w) & "x" & show (box.lr-h) & "  laid root " & show (lb.lr-x) & "," & show (lb.lr-y) & " " & show (lb.lr-w) & "x" & show (lb.lr-h))
      let mx = poke-32 blk dk-wnd-st-cell dk-wnd-st-max
      in let st = dk-wnd-st blk
      in let ws2 = ui-wscale dss-big-w
      in let bh = dk-wnd-bar-h gfont-none ws2
      in let bx = dk-wnd-content desk-focus-sheet dss-big-w dss-big-h ds gfont-none ws2
      in print-line-uni ("maximised frame tree box " & show (dk-wnd-rx blk dss-big-w st ds) & "," & show (dk-wnd-ry blk dss-big-w dss-big-h st ds + bh) & " " & show (dk-wnd-rw blk dss-big-w st ds) & "x" & show (dk-wnd-rh blk dss-big-w dss-big-h st ds - bh))
      print-line-uni ("and the pane's own body box " & show (bx.lr-x) & "," & show (bx.lr-y) & " " & show (bx.lr-w) & "x" & show (bx.lr-h))
      let big = alloc-zeroed (dss-big-w * dss-big-h * 4) 64
      in let painted = desk-sheet-body big dss-big-w dss-big-h dss-big-w font gfont-none ds edited
      in let sbig = ui-wscale dss-big-w
      in let hx = dss-centre-x painted (gsh-cell-id 2 1) * sbig
      in let hy = dss-centre-y painted (gsh-cell-id 2 1) * sbig
      in let want = 2 * gsh-cols-shown + 1
      in act
        print-line-uni ("the painter puts C3 at " & show hx & "," & show hy & " and the hit test answers cell " & show (desk-sheet-hit dss-big-w dss-big-h hx hy ds gfont-none edited) & ", wanted " & show want)
        print-line-uni ("laid at the screen corner the same point answers cell " & show (desk-sheet-hit dss-big-w dss-big-h (hx - bx.lr-x) (hy - bx.lr-y) ds gfont-none edited))
        let s2 = ui-wscale dss-big-w
        in let hl = widget-layout (gsh-tree edited) (dk-theme-ds ds) (layout-rect (bx.lr-x / s2) (bx.lr-y / s2) (bx.lr-w / s2) (bx.lr-h / s2))
        in let hr = hl.wn-bounds
        in print-line-uni ("the hit lay puts its root at " & show (hr.lr-x) & "," & show (hr.lr-y) & " " & show (hr.lr-w) & "x" & show (hr.lr-h) & " and C3 at " & show (dss-centre-x hl (gsh-cell-id 2 1)) & "," & show (dss-centre-y hl (gsh-cell-id 2 1)) & " against the point " & show (comp-hit-x hx s2) & "," & show (comp-hit-y hy s2))
        print-line-uni ("and the focused cell carries the accent tone: " & show (dss-tone painted (gsh-cell-id (edited.sp-row) (edited.sp-col))) & " against " & show (dss-tone painted (gsh-cell-id 0 0)) & " for an unfocused one")
        let typing = DeskApps { da-files = None, da-browser = None, da-scene = None, da-edit = None, da-sheet = Just (gsh-pane-new 0), da-review = None }
        in let sp2 = when typing.da-sheet
          is Just (p) -> p
          is None -> gsh-pane-new 0
        in let f1 = __record-set sp2 "sp-row" 2
        in let f2 = __record-set sp2 "sp-col" 1
        in act
          print-line-uni ("B3 starts at " & dss-cell-text sp2 2 1 & " and D3 at " & dss-cell-text sp2 2 3)
          print-line-uni ("scancode 10 types [" & utf8-bytes-to-text (list-push [] (apply-mods (scancode-to-keycode 10) 0)) & "], the key answering " & show (desk-sheet-key typing 10 0))
          print-line-uni ("while editing, the cell shows the buffer: [" & gsh-cell-text (sp2.sp-sheet) (eval-run ((sp2.sp-sheet).sh-prog)) 2 1 (sp2.sp-row) (sp2.sp-col) (sp2.sp-buf) & "]")
          print-line-uni ("backspace answers " & show (desk-sheet-key typing 14 0) & " and empties the buffer, so a second answers " & show (desk-sheet-key typing 14 0))
          print-line-uni ("Enter on an empty buffer answers " & show (desk-sheet-key typing 28 0) & ", which is what stops it clearing the cell")
          let t1 = desk-sheet-key typing 10 0
          in let t2 = desk-sheet-key typing 28 0
          in print-line-uni ("typing 9 and committing: B3 = " & dss-cell-text sp2 2 1 & " and D3 = " & dss-cell-text sp2 2 3)
          let fb = alloc-zeroed (dss-big-w * dss-big-h * 4) 64
          in let bb = alloc-zeroed (dss-big-w * dss-big-h * 4) 64
          in let blk2 = desk-wnd-blk desk-focus-sheet ds
          in let st2 = dk-wnd-st blk2
          in let ws3 = ui-wscale dss-big-w
          in let f = dk-wnd-frame fb dss-big-w dss-big-h dss-big-w font gfont-none (gsh-tree edited) "Sheets" ds (dk-wnd-rx blk2 dss-big-w st2 ds) (dk-wnd-ry blk2 dss-big-w dss-big-h st2 ds) (dk-wnd-rw blk2 dss-big-w st2 ds) (dk-wnd-rh blk2 dss-big-w dss-big-h st2 ds) True
          in let g = desk-sheet-body bb dss-big-w dss-big-h dss-big-w font gfont-none ds edited
          in act
            print-line-uni ("SHEET-13, the same pixel down each road:")
            print-line-uni (dss-row-of fb bb 400)
            print-line-uni (dss-row-of fb bb 800)
            print-line-uni (dss-row-of fb bb 812)
            print-line-uni (dss-row-of fb bb 818)
            print-line-uni (dss-row-of fb bb 823)
            print-line-uni (dss-row-of fb bb 830)
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
